# Lisp sources must keep LF line endings on every platform.
#
# FORMAT's line-continuation directive is `~' followed by a *newline*.  With
# CRLF the next character is a Return, which is not a directive at all, so
# every format string that wraps across lines fails to compile -- and this
# codebase has dozens.  Git on Windows converts to CRLF on checkout by
# default, which is how the first Windows CI run died in src/conditions.lisp,
# a file with no platform-specific code in it whatsoever.
*.lisp text eol=lf
*.asd  text eol=lf

# Keep everything else the tests read byte-for-byte as committed.
*.md   text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
